    "body": "## Problem\r\nSee #39683.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nRewrite in Lua.",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-13T00:06:17Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40675#discussion_r3559849633"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/40675"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3559849633"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Repeating my comments from @barrettruth's PR: Since `matchit` is enabled by default in Neovim, there is no point is cargo-culting Vim's opt plugin structure:\n1. put everything directly under `runtime/`\n2. inline the `enable()` call in `plugin/matchit.lua` -- only `require` inside functions that are called conditionally, otherwise you pay the overhead for cached modules without any gains\n3. leave the vimscript plugin in opt but add a step that disables the new Lua plugin when `packadd`ing it -- this way, people unhappy with the new version can keep using the legacy version (and any plugin that depends on it), freeing us to implement the new version as a \"sane reboot\".",
            "commit_id": "1e519ae888be35891c765b49e5c2befb1b9c2c49",
            "created_at": "2026-07-10T14:55:15Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+-- Nvim: load the matchit plugin by default.\n+if vim.g.loaded_matchit == nil and vim.o.packpath:find(vim.env.VIMRUNTIME, 1, true) then\n+  vim.cmd.packadd('matchit')\n+end",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40675#discussion_r3559849633",
            "id": 3559849633,
            "line": 4,
            "node_id": "PRRC_kwDOAPphoM7ULv6h",
